from pathlib import Path
import html,json,math
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
load=lambda n:json.loads((R/n).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
d=load('RESULTS.json');q=load('QUALIFICATION.json');e=lambda x:html.escape(str(x))
def table(h,rs):return '<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+e(x)+'</th>' for x in h)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+str(v)+'</td>' for v in row)+'</tr>' for row in rs)+'</tbody></table></div>'
body='<p class="muted">VOYNICH · EXACT TRANSITION CONTROL · v96</p><h1>What remains after preserving local transitions?</h1><p class="notice">No one-word-gap result passes the retained opening-search correction. Starred text retains a modest uncorrected residual; baths do not. The exact null has genuine variation and sufficient numerical resolution, so this is not the old Monte Carlo rank-floor failure. It still does not prove that local transitions completely explain the text.</p>'
body+='<p>Bath hand2/B/P and Starred hand3/B/P, H/F separate on the same shared source loci as v78. S=sh- opening, Q=qok- opening, N=other readable word. Unknown slots split spans; no words are deleted, merged or joined across gaps.</p>'
body+='<h2>What this control holds fixed</h2><p>Within each readable source span it fixes the literal first/last words, complete word multiset and every directed adjacent S/Q/N transition count. It enumerates uniformly compatible class orders, with a constant number of literal-word assignments per class order. Adjacent sh/qok ordering is therefore fixed by construction; this analysis cannot retest or erase the v77 adjacent result.</p><p>This preserves opening-class transitions, not exact word bigrams or character junctions. Pinning each span endpoint is also stronger than the earlier line shuffle. It is one focused conditional model, not a complete account of syntax, orthography or copying.</p>'
body+='<h2>Exact qualification before corpus scoring</h2>'+table(['Check','Result'],[['Authored class sequences',q['authored_sequences']],['Distinct fixed-transition fibers',q['fibers']],['Exact DP view checks',q['DP_view_checks']],['Exact DP vs enumeration / rational rank bounds','PASS'],['Distinct neutral-word assignment multiplicity','Constant; verified'],['Repeated two-path fiber vs exact binomial convolution','PASS, 1–128 informative spans'],['Worst-case correction budget',q['worst_case_correction']],['All-positive 32-span corrected p',f'{q["all_positive32_corrected_p"]:.8f}'],['Frozen qualification gates',e(q['status'])]])
body+='<p>Two authored class orders, S N N Q N S and S N Q N N S, have identical adjacent transitions and endpoints but opposite gap scores. Independent copies supply a known exact higher-order alternative. These are implementation/calibration controls, not independent historical labels or a guarantee of corpus-specific power.</p><details><summary>Every power-control outcome, including low-power cases</summary>'+table(['Informative spans','Probability of positive conditional path','Exact positive-direction rejection probability'],[[x['informative_spans'],e(x['positive_path_probability']),f'{x["power"]:.8f}'] for x in q['power_grid']])+'</details><p>Gates required ≥80% power at 128 informative spans with positive-path probability .80, and ≥90% at .95; both passed. At smaller sample sizes or weaker effects, power can be poor, as retained above.</p>'
body+='<h2>Residual one-word-gap ordering</h2>'
rows=[]
for p in d['panels']:
 for v in p['views']:
  if v['status']!='complete':rows.append([e(p['section']),p['reading'],v['view'],'BLOCKED',e(v['reason']),'','','','','']);continue
  x=v['result'];rows.append([e(p['section'])+' / '+p['hand'],p['reading'],e(v['view']),x['observed_D'],f'{x["conditional_mean"]:.3f}',f'{x["conditional_SD"]:.3f}',e(x['null_95']),f'{x["raw_two_sided_p"]:.6f}',f'{x["corrected_p"]:.6f}',str(v['variable_score_spans'])+'/'+str(p['spans'])])
body+=table(['Stratum','Reading','Middle definition','Observed D','Transition-null mean D','Null SD','95% null range','Raw exact p','Full corrected p','Variable-score spans'],rows)
body+='<p>D=#sh X qok minus #qok X sh. Primary any_middle includes every readable middle word; non_target_middle requires middle N. Observed D is independently verified identical to v78. The conditional baseline changes because local transitions now remain fixed.</p><p>Each raw p is an exact two-sided tail ordered by distance from its exact conditional mean. Correction multiplies by the original number of prefix-pair candidates in that panel and by28 (historical14panels ×2views). This is a conservative Bonferroni bound, not a claim to have computed all other exact prefix-pair distributions. It changes the correction statistic from v77 maxT while retaining the full family budget. All other scores remain definable under this same fixed conditional word-order null.</p>'
body+='<h2>Mobility, conditioning and numerical resolution</h2>'
rows=[]
for p in d['panels']:
 for v in p['views']:
  if v['status']!='complete':continue
  x=v['result'];rows.append([e(p['section']),p['reading'],v['view'],v['alternative_class_order_spans'],v['variable_score_spans'],x['support_values'],f'{x["minimum_attainable_corrected_p"]:.3g}', 'yes' if x['can_reject_at_05'] else 'NO: insufficient conditional resolution',max(s['memo_states'] for s in v['span_records'])])
body+=table(['Section','Reading','View','Alternative-order spans','Variable-score spans','Total null support values','Smallest possible corrected p','Can resolve .05?','Max span memo states'],rows)
body+='<p>Most spans contribute no score variation, but each panel retains hundreds that do. Exact histogram convolution uses integer counts, not MCMC or Monte Carlo estimates. Any frozen exact-solver budget failure would block the whole affected panel rather than drop difficult spans; no such truncation is used.</p>'
body+='<h2>Source exceptions and folio contributions</h2><p>All source span records, class edges, one-path cases and exact hexadecimal integer weights are preserved in RESULTS.json and NULL-DISTRIBUTIONS.json. Selected deviations below are descriptive displays, not newly discovered significant examples.</p>'
for p in d['panels']:
 for v in p['views']:
  if v['status']!='complete':continue
  fs={}
  for s in v['span_records']:
   hist={int(k):int(n,16) for k,n in s['score_support'].items()};total=sum(hist.values());mu=sum(k*n for k,n in hist.items())/total;f=fs.setdefault(s['folio'],dict(observed=0,expected=0.,variable=0));f['observed']+=s['observed_D'];f['expected']+=mu;f['variable']+=len(hist)>1
  body+='<details><summary>'+e(p['section']+' · '+p['reading']+' · '+v['view'])+'</summary>'+table(['Folio','Observed D','Conditional expected D','Residual','Variable spans'],[[e(f),x['observed'],f'{x["expected"]:.3f}',f'{x["observed"]-x["expected"]:.3f}',x['variable']] for f,x in sorted(fs.items())])
  body+='<details><summary>Every source span, including fixed and reverse cases</summary>'
  for s in v['span_records']:
   hist={int(k):int(n,16) for k,n in s['score_support'].items()};mu=sum(k*n for k,n in hist.items())/sum(hist.values());body+='<article><p><strong>'+e(s['locator'])+'</strong> · span starts '+str(s['start_ordinal'])+' · D '+str(s['observed_D'])+' · expected '+f'{mu:.3f}'+' · score support '+e(sorted(hist))+'</p><p class="raw">'+e(' '.join(s['tokens']))+'</p></article>'
  body+='</details></details>'
body+='<h2>Interpretation</h2><p>Baths offer no unusual residual. Starred text remains suggestive before correction, particularly with a non-target middle, but no view passes the complete search budget. This does not establish equivalence to the local model, and it does not identify the cause of the adjacent preference. Moderate residual effects may remain undetected under this conservative correction.</p><p>The earlier adjacent result is conditioned on and preserved. Neither it nor these residuals identify operations, attributes, timing or word meanings. H/F are alternate readings; shared traditions, line structure and copying remain possible influences. No global semantic or grammar qualification is claimed.</p><p><a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen control and gates</a> · <a href="QUALIFICATION.json">All qualification outcomes</a> · <a href="RESULTS.json">All source spans and panels</a> · <a href="NULL-DISTRIBUTIONS.json">Exact integer null weights</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Independent numerical checks</a> · <a href="../one-gap-order-v78/report.html">Preserved v78</a> · <a href="../opening-maxT-qualification-v77/report.html">Preserved adjacent result</a></p><p>Browser appearance remains unreviewed; exact/source checks are separate.</p>'
css='''<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark;--bg:light-dark(#f5f2e9,#18251f);--fg:light-dark(#203f35,#e2e9df);--sub:light-dark(#54695b,#b4c7b7);--rule:light-dark(#c0ccbd,#48604d);--fill:light-dark(#e5ebda,#2a3e2d)}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1450px;padding:30px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:32px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:23px;margin-top:30px}p{max-width:1100px}a{color:inherit}.muted{color:var(--sub)}.notice{padding:16px;background:var(--fill)}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.raw{font:15px/1.8 ui-monospace,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}article{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}summary{cursor:pointer}details{margin:16px 0}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:16px}}</style>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Exact local-transition control · v96</title>'+css+'</head><body><main>'+body+'</main></body></html>',encoding='utf-8');print('Transition-control report written.')
